Parts of the `elgrep` crate are copied from ripgrep, at commit
48b0c795f4feb37343b2832d991c5c6a3900c08a (ripgrep 15.1.0), and are used under
the MIT license reproduced below. ripgrep is dual licensed under MIT or the
Unlicense; this project takes it under MIT and keeps the notice.

The copied code is the command line facade and the search path it drives:
argument definitions and parsing, help and man page rendering, the searcher
and printer wiring, haystack discovery, logging, and messages. Everything
under `crates/eg/src/index`, and the `sngram`, `sngram-types` and
`sngram-train` packages, are this project's own work.

Upstream: https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep

